ound for 15 years  uh wikipedia which is everybody's first  place to look up anything  uh only came on in 2001. now you can say  that it's not always accurate but  there's always something there and you  can skip wikipedia but it is there and  if we have an argument how many people  live there or whatever  it's there and it's free and it's only  been around since 2001. if we look at  the speed with which we can access these  different systems i mean i can remember  standing in japan selling lumber  connecting on a public telephone taking  forever you know so that i can send  information but i can work in the rain  whatever and now we have here i am  i am standing here and i'm connected  and that's all happened in  in a very very short space of time and  so the more people are connected the  more the ideas are being developed and  the faster these things are  are accelerating uh if we look at this  you know we used to deal with mainframe  computers desktop  laptop ipad iphone everything's getting  smaller  uh  even the content is merging now you know  radio uh  internet telephone skype communicate  it's all merging into one it's  extraordinary you'll be able to to dial  into whatever like i can sit at home  on my  apple  and i can go to a radio station and i  can look up classical music and up opens  up you know 100 radio stations and i  want to there's radio chopin there's  radio mozart there's barack whatever i  want i pick one that happens to be a  radio station out of geneva  uh i have in my house i got a little  repeater station for my  for my  network  and i have speakers on there  and so just before i sit down for  breakfast on a sunday morning i like  barack music with my breakfast  so before we sit down i just pop in a  radio station we listen to baroque music  while we have breakfast it's  extraordinary if i wanted to listen to  portuguese photos i could find them so  uh so all of this stuff is happening  and uh  just to get back to  our friend the rational